questionvariables.text:
/* Shared Question Bank Place Value, Rounding and Standard Form PVRS-07
Conceptual task: convert standard form to an ordinary large whole number.
Conceptual reference only: NUMBAS-114888.
The source licence is not verified for direct adaptation, so this STACK question is independently authored.
No source wording or mathematical content is copied. */
/* Generate a valid coefficient with exactly three significant digits. */
d1: rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
d2: rand_with_prohib(0,9,[]);
d3: rand_with_prohib(1,9,[]);
coefficient: d1 + d2/10 + d3/100;
/* Use positive exponents large enough to produce whole numbers. */
exponent: rand_with_prohib(4,7,[]);
/* Convert exactly to a whole number.
Because coefficient has two decimal places, its integer representation is multiplied by 10^(exponent-2). */
mantissa_integer: d1*100 + d2*10 + d3;
answer: mantissa_integer * 10^(exponent-2);
/* Primary misconception: move decimal point in the wrong direction.
This corresponds to multiplying by 10^(-exponent). */
wrong_direction: coefficient / 10^exponent;
/* Secondary misconception: move the decimal point one place too few. */
wrong_one_fewer: mantissa_integer * 10^(exponent-3);
/* Display coefficient as decimal. */
coefficient_display: float(coefficient);
